{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792591233,"nonce":"TmB1XU83YHhR9xQMSbdafS3JTXA=","title":"ChimpMonk on wasm as a GC testbed: pauses against a 60 fps frame budget in a crowded 3D physics scene","message":"ChimpMonk has no wasm target yet. Its physics engine and animation in a browser, with a crowded 3D scene, would be the allocation-heavy, frame-budgeted case ash's wasm collector has not been measured on.\n\nWhy it matters. Every full-collection pause measured in a real app is above a 16.6 ms frame: the ashui dashboard in Chrome (4 laps, 13 collections in 48 s) paused 9 to 31 ms at 44 to 177 MB live, about 0.5 percent of run time but a visible hitch. A crowded scene allocates vectors and contacts every frame and holds a larger live set, so pauses would be more frequent and longer. The design limits that would show:\n- stop-the-world, whole-live-set marking, not incremental or concurrent;\n- on wasm a collection runs only at a compiled poll (wasm locals are invisible to the collector), so a long step without a poll delays it;\n- linear memory only grows, so the heap high-water mark stays;\n- conservative scanning on wasm32 (the precise class-layout scan reduces false pins).\n\nNot compared: ash has no WasmGC backend, so there is no measurement against an engine-managed collector. A comparison would need a hand-ported kernel.\n\nWhat to measure once the target exists (or first, natively, with the same scene):\n1. ASH_GC_STATS=1 pause histogram against 16.6 ms over a scripted camera fly-through at several body counts.\n2. Collections per second and the heap high-water mark.\n3. Frame-time percentiles from the page, to see whether pauses become dropped frames.\n\nPossible remedies if pauses are the problem: smaller young sets and fewer full collections kept off the frame path; pooling vectors and contacts in ChimpMonk; collecting at the end of a frame or when idle; incremental marking if the rest is not enough.\n\nRelated: d1961ff (GC trigger policy and idle collection for UI apps), 859f6d5 (wasm collections, closed).","files":null}]}